# check: run
# L12/L12a: an exponent is one only when a digit follows its "e" and sign ("1e_x" is the number 1 and the name e_x - it
# was "1e" and "_x", with a separator reported). A second "." before a name is a member access on the float, which
# e13cfloat.olang shows refused by E13c, not reported as a second decimal point
fn main() ? {
    e_x := 3
    assert 1e2 + 1E-1 == 100.1 and e_x == 3
}
